# Base system, desktop environment, and infrastructure common to every mode.
# Keep this list to what's genuinely required at all times — everything else
# belongs in a category-specific list so the default ISO doesn't balloon
# (spec section 21).

task-kde-desktop
plasma-workspace
sddm
network-manager
network-manager-gnome
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree

# Live-environment core
live-boot
live-config
live-tools

# D-Bus / policykit — required by mode-manager and security-center
dbus
policykit-1
python3-dbus
python3-gi
gir1.2-glib-2.0
gir1.2-gtk-4.0
gir1.2-adw-1

# NOTE: mode-manager and security-center are written against `pydbus`.
# I have NOT verified python3-pydbus is a real bookworm package name —
# pydbus is often pip-only. If apt can't find it, either pip-install into
# a venv via a chroot hook, or port both apps to python3-dbus (already
# listed above) + GLib mainloop instead, which is stdlib-adjacent and
# definitely available. Flagging rather than guessing.

# Firewall backend used by Mode Manager
nftables

# Disk/encryption tooling needed for persistence + Emergency Shutdown
cryptsetup
parted
gparted

# isolinux/syslinux-common/syslinux-utils: required INSIDE the target
# chroot, not just on the CI runner. live-build's bundled BIOS
# bootloader theme (used even though --bootloaders is set to grub-efi —
# a hybrid ISO needs BOTH BIOS and UEFI boot paths, and live-build adds
# isolinux for the BIOS side unconditionally) copies its theme files
# into the chroot, then dereferences symlinks WITHIN the chroot's own
# filesystem
# (`Chroot chroot cp -aL ...`, confirmed by reading
# /usr/lib/live/build/lb_binary_syslinux directly) — so the real
# isolinux.bin/vesamenu.c32 files these symlinks point to must actually
# exist inside the built system, not just on the machine running the
# build. See build-iso.yml/update.yml's "Patch live-build isolinux theme
# paths" step for the other half of this fix — this live-build version's
# bundled symlinks also point to a pre-reorg path
# (/usr/lib/syslinux/isolinux.bin) that no longer exists in current
# Debian packaging (real path is /usr/lib/ISOLINUX/isolinux.bin,
# capitalized directory) — same "old live-build, new Debian archive
# layout" bug pattern as the Contents-<arch>.gz and bookworm/updates
# fixes already applied elsewhere in this repo. syslinux-utils added
# for the same underlying reason: `isohybrid` (needed by
# lb_binary_iso's generated binary.sh, also run via `Chroot chroot`)
# lives in syslinux-utils, not the bare "syslinux" package live-build's
# own Check_package call assumes — confirmed directly by installing
# syslinux-utils and checking its actual file list.
isolinux
syslinux-common
syslinux-utils
e2fsprogs
util-linux
# lsblk/wipefs/findmnt ship inside util-linux — not separate packages,
# not listed individually to avoid an apt error on a nonexistent name.
